<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis IV, Landgrave of Thuringia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1200–<a href="/years/1227">1227</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis IV was Landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> from 1217 to 1227, a son of Hermann I, patron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> poets. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-of-hungary">Elizabeth of Hungary</a>, who became famous for her charity and was canonised in 1235. A supporter of Emperor Frederick II, he joined the emperor's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> but died of illness at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otranto">Otranto</a> in 1227 before sailing. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-raspe">Henry Raspe</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-iv-landgrave-of-thuringia.jpg" alt="Louis IV, Landgrave of Thuringia" width="143" height="122" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludvik4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
